Iranian state television: Foreign Minister Araghchi met U.S. envoy Steve Witkoff on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly, a meeting Washington asked for. Tehran agreed in order to pass along its conditions for reopening the Strait of Hormuz.
@Osint613

The conditions: immediate lifting of the naval blockade, immediate release of all frozen Iranian funds, and an end to the war on all resistance fronts.

IRGC spokesman Hossein Mohabbi on Trump's warnings:

"One of his habits is that he threatens constantly, and forgets that he has already made threats in the past that he was unable to carry out, and then comes back and makes more threats. If the United States tries to attack any place in Iran, not only Mount Makush, not only the place it threatened, we are fully prepared and will stand up to the American attack."
@Osint613
